  "0": [
   {
    "context": "John 17, 17. Sanctify them by your truth. Your word is truth. In this passage, Jesus is praying to God the Father and asks God to sanctify or to separate his people by his truth. Starting with truth just feels a little insidious. Actually, uncovering truth should be a lifelong venture where you explore the world and uncover different ideas, and your concept of truth should evolve over time. Now, of course, an insular religion doesn't exactly want you doing that, which is why I could see it opening this extended metaphor by trying to rein in the idea of truth.",
    "dist": 0.4285,
    "occurrence_id": 4424,
    "published_at": "2024-03-07T21:00:06Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "truth",
    "t": 265.28,
    "title": "The Armor of God is Stupid",
    "video_id": "3F_IZAOnqBA"
   },
   {
    "context": "And it seems to me that if we are to present Christianity to thinking men and women in such a culture, it's absolutely vital that we be able to give reasons for thinking that it's really the truth.",
    "dist": 0.432,
    "occurrence_id": 18701,
    "published_at": "2014-12-22T15:04:16Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "truth",
    "t": 61.92,
    "title": "What is the Importance of Scholarship in the Christian World?",
    "video_id": "IS020H72Qq0"
   },
   {
    "context": "It's equated with Christ. So really you're starting by strapping on Jesus, who is called the truth. Either way, it makes truth a possession and not a process. Just encouraging one to signal certainty that they really don't have over any kind of intellectual humility or I don't know.",
    "dist": 0.434,
    "occurrence_id": 31297,
    "published_at": "2025-09-30T14:00:53Z",
    "role": "unattributed",
    "surface": "truth",
    "t": 545.72,
    "title": "The Armor of God Deconstructed & Rebuilt with Reason!",
    "video_id": "Vxh1R5jHoMM"
   },
   {
    "context": "And a God worthy of worship, I think would would understand that. So, no, I'm not afraid of God's wrath. And that's the thing about Christianity and and why it breeds atheism, is it it teaches you that truth is good and worth pursuing and that morality matters, and then when you develop those skills, it ends up turning on Christianity itself. And so that's like the poetic tragedy of it: that Christianity teaches you to value truth, that truth will set you free, that honesty and integrity matters, that knocking and seeking will lead to finding.",
    "dist": 0.4357,
    "occurrence_id": 46062,
    "published_at": "2025-08-04T15:00:06Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "truth",
